# 8. MOTION AND INTERACTION ENGINEERING

The website needs sophisticated motion, but not every element should move constantly.

Create a consistent motion system with reusable timing values, easing curves, and animation variants.

Prefer one coherent animation approach over an unnecessary collection of overlapping libraries.

Use Motion for React for most interface animations. Add GSAP/ScrollTrigger only if a specific effect genuinely requires more advanced timeline or pinned-scroll control and the current environment supports it cleanly.

Use the lightest practical implementation.

## Required animations

### A. Initial entrance

Create a polished introduction sequence:

- Navigation enters with restrained movement.
- The headline reveals through a clip-path or mask animation.
- Supporting copy appears in a controlled stagger.
- Calls to action enter with subtle movement.
- The hero visual responds gently to the cursor or scroll.

The sequence must remain short enough that users can start interacting immediately.

Do not require a long full-screen loading animation before the visitor can use the website.

### B. Typography motion

Implement one or two tasteful kinetic typography treatments, such as:

- Staggered word reveals
- Subtle text displacement
- An understated repeating marquee
- An occasional character scramble used for small labels

Avoid unreadable rapid scrambling and constant movement that makes the page feel unstable.

### C. Scroll-driven storytelling

Use intersection-based reveals, restrained parallax, and carefully selected scroll-synchronized effects.

A pinned sequence is acceptable for one signature moment, but do not pin every section.

Ensure content remains reachable if JavaScript animation fails or reduced motion is enabled.

### D. Project-card interaction

Use:

- Gentle perspective or tilt on suitable desktop pointers
- Image or visual clipping reveals
- Subtle title movement
- Controlled depth
- Clear keyboard and touch interaction

Keep animation performant and avoid recalculating expensive layouts on every pointer event.

### E. Navigation and page transitions

Animate between homepage sections and individual project pages.

Transitions must not interfere with browser navigation, keyboard access, focus management, route loading, or direct links to a project detail page.

If the router changes, ensure scroll position and focus behavior remain predictable.

### F. Custom cursor

Implement a contextual cursor follower only on devices with a fine pointer and hover support.

Do not replace or hide the native pointer on touch devices.

It must not cover interactive targets, interfere with clicks, or become a dependency for operating the website.

### G. Parallax and depth

Use restrained background layers and depth cues to support the cinematic aesthetic.

Avoid expensive full-screen canvas redraws when CSS transforms or static SVG artwork achieve the same effect.

### H. Optional 3D/WebGL scene

Consider one distinctive 3D, Canvas, or WebGL element only if it materially improves the creative concept.

Prefer a lightweight animated form with a graceful static fallback.

Lazy-load expensive libraries and avoid loading a heavy 3D scene before the main content becomes usable.

### I. Optional sound

Sound effects must be disabled by default.

Never autoplay music or surprise the visitor with sound.

If sound is implemented, make it opt-in, easily muted, and entirely unnecessary for navigation or content comprehension.

## Reduced-motion behavior

Support `prefers-reduced-motion`.

When reduced motion is enabled:

- Disable nonessential parallax and continuous movement.
- Remove or simplify large scroll-linked sequences.
- Replace complex entrances with quick, readable transitions.
- Preserve all content, navigation, and actions.
- Avoid flashes and motion that may cause discomfort.

Use transforms and opacity when practical, respect touch devices, and keep the interface functional even when all optional animation is removed.

